{"skill":{"slug":"skills-search","displayName":"Skills.sh Search"},"version":{"version":"1.0.4","createdAt":1768970984785,"changelog":"Added --popular flag to show top skills by installs","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3198,"sha256":"9e1bc5989af8f68aa4430b11f782f24f6ca0abad15112d46d253bf2c54da659b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"cli.js","size":2746,"sha256":"e5d9b6fee97db30e4ae3a4c07a934e1adb2853a197bdb6e02f9b953f977f435e","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"package.json","size":422,"sha256":"89c02575e132d7c85b7db102a9dd57d68a674a15a3e3cb3015ddb4e38e26e713","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1882,"sha256":"73cb8eb61f7884594268f56d253cea123ba8ec66b330de19c00814ee463472a3","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789016804261,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"253b416ac7cec8f067937875ed177d4c29a9dce873ec80042632ea98e0b550be","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/253b416ac7cec8f067937875ed177d4c29a9dce873ec80042632ea98e0b550be","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: skills-search\nVersion: 1.0.4\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. Its primary function, as implemented in `cli.js`, is to query the official `https://skills.sh/api/skills` endpoint to search for and display skills. The `SKILL.md` instructions guide the agent on how to use this search functionality and subsequently install other skills using `npx skills add`, which is a legitimate follow-up action for a skill search tool. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or prompt injection attempts to mislead the agent into harmful actions. The `ls` command is for verifying installation, not exfiltration.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159816799},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":53,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":8,"checkedAt":1789016804261},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a small skill-search CLI whose behavior is disclosed and purpose-aligned, with supply-chain and terminal-output risks users should handle cautiously.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Runtime behavior is proportionate for a registry search tool: Node HTTPS access to skills.sh and terminal output; no local file reads, credential access, destructive actions, or privilege escalation were found.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The Clawdbot install path is disclosed as clawdhub install skills-search; documentation also shows unpinned npx commands, which are a supply-chain hygiene issue but not evidence of malicious intent.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Instructions include examples for installing discovered skills, but they are visible user-directed steps rather than hidden or automatic agent behavior.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence mechanisms, background workers, services, startup hooks, memory writes, or privilege changes were present in the inspected artifacts.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is searching the skills.sh registry, and the CLI only fetches that API, filters results, and prints matching skills and optional install commands.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing or using --show-install output, review the discovered skill source, prefer pinned package versions where possible, and do not copy terminal-generated install commands unless the repository name looks valid and trusted.","findings":"[AE1] expected: The flagged references are ordinary documentation references to SKILL.md files and example repositories; the package contents were locally available and inspected, so this did not support analysis evasion.\n[RP1] expected: The unpinned npx examples are real and should be improved, but they are disclosed installation examples for a skill-discovery workflow and do not cause automatic execution by this skill.\n[T08] expected: The SARIF supply-chain concern is valid guidance for users because npx resolves mutable packages, but artifact evidence shows user-invoked example commands rather than hidden remote payload execution.\n[T09] expected: The CLI prints registry-provided names and sources without validation, including copyable install commands. This is a real terminal-spoofing or copy-paste risk, but the CLI does not execute those generated commands itself.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789016804261}}}}}